{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% cap on the Annual General Adjustment","requirement":"The Rent Board may not approve an Annual General Adjustment above 5%, even if the Rent Ordinance's CPI formula would produce a higher figure; banked unused AGAs from prior years may still be applied to reach the rent ceiling.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units in Berkeley whose annual rent increase is set by the Rent Board's Annual General Adjustment.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Fully covered rental units in Berkeley, including most multifamily properties built before 1980"},"exemptions":"Does not prevent a landlord from applying banked (unused) AGAs from previous years to raise rent above 5% up to the rent ceiling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB coverage of government-owned or subsidized units","requirement":"Government-owned or government-subsidized rental units such as Section 8 and Shelter Plus Care are now fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance and must be registered with the Rent Board; fully covered units get a rent ceiling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Government-owned or -subsidized units including Housing Choice Voucher (Section 8), Shelter Plus Care, VASH, LIHTC, HOME and City Housing Trust Fund; fully or partially covered depending on unit type and on whether federal or state law bars rent control.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units listed in the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":"Units are partially covered rather than fully covered where federal law, state law or administrative regulation prohibits rent control, such as Section 202 and Section 811 units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units become either fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB narrows the shared kitchen or bath exemption","requirement":"A unit where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath with the landlord is exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy; otherwise the unit is covered.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units in Berkeley in which the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Units where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath with the landlord"},"exemptions":"Units where the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB limits capital improvement petitions to completed work","requirement":"A landlord may petition for a rent increase only for completed capital improvements; the landlord can no longer petition to have rent increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units in Berkeley where a landlord seeks a rent increase for capital improvements.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Fully covered rental units; capital improvement rent increase petitions"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"Landlords can only file a petition for rent increases for completed capital improvements (they can no longer petition to have rent increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB minimum rental debt for nonpayment eviction","requirement":"A landlord may not evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent unless the tenant owes at least one month's Fair Market Rent for a unit of equivalent size in the Oakland-Fremont HUD metro area.","key_value":"1 month's FMR","coverage_conditions":"Rental units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance, where just cause is required to evict.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"Eviction for nonpayment of rent is no longer permitted for rental debt of less than one month’s Fair Market Rent for a unit of equivalent size.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB bars eviction for refusing to sign a similar lease","requirement":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance, where just cause is required to evict.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB requirements for lease-breach evictions","requirement":"To evict for a lease breach, the landlord must clearly describe the alleged breach, must show the tenant's behavior was unreasonable and that the breach caused actual harm, and may not evict for breaches causing no actual harm.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance, where just cause is required to evict.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"In any notice terminating a tenancy for a lease breach, the landlord must clearly describe the alleged breach. The landlord must demonstrate that the tenant’s behavior was unreasonable, and may not evict tenants for lease breaches that do not cause the landlord any actual harm.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB eviction notice content and Rent Board filing deadline","requirement":"Eviction notices must tell tenants that advice about the notice is available from the Rent Board, and the landlord must file copies of eviction notices and eviction lawsuits with the Rent Board within three business days of serving the tenant.","key_value":"3 business days","coverage_conditions":"Rental units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance, where just cause is required to evict.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"Eviction notices must contain certain information directing tenants to the Rent Board, and copies of eviction notices and eviction lawsuits must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days of serving the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB annual adjustment of owner move-in relocation assistance","requirement":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments each year to the owner move-in eviction relocation assistance amounts paid to tenants.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Owner move-in evictions of tenants in rental units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance (Measure BB)","quoted_span":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance amounts each year.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
